2. User Materials and Application Output

For purposes of this license, "User Materials" means player names,
player settings, key bindings, window state, custom crosshair data,
imported skins, world edits, save data, Othello settings, user-created
text, user-created images, user-created video, chat content, AI
workbench history, and other materials that a user independently
creates, inputs, edits, records, or prepares through ordinary use of the
Ludoxel application.

For purposes of this license, "Application Output" means ordinary
screenshots, screen recordings, save files, logs, generated AI
workbench records, rendered states, configuration files, and other
output produced by the Ludoxel application through ordinary application
use.

User Materials do not become Original Materials merely because the user
entered, edited, generated, saved, exported, displayed, or shared them
by using the Ludoxel application.

Subject to this license and any applicable third-party rights, users may
use, record, reproduce, publish, and share their own User Materials and
Application Output, including ordinary screenshots, screen recordings,
save data, and user-created AI workbench output.

The permission stated in this Section 2 does not grant any right to
copy, reuse, modify, distribute, deploy, incorporate, relicense, sell,
create derivative works from, represent as one's own, or use as
training data any Original Materials, including source code,
implementation text, documentation, repository text, build materials,
shaders, bundled resources, visual assets, project-specific textures,
branding material, application icons, user interface assets, or any
substantially derived work based on them.

If User Materials or Application Output contain, reproduce, or
incorporate a material part of the Original Materials, third-party
materials, repository text, user interface text, visual assets, bundled
resources, project-specific textures, branding material, application
icons, or other protected repository content, that included protected
